# Store text with LF in the repository and check it out with LF everywhere.
#
# Our containers and CI runners are Linux. A file committed with CRLF that ends
# up as a shell script inside a container fails with "bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M",
# which is a genuinely confusing hour to lose. Normalising here also silences
# git's "LF will be replaced by CRLF" warnings on Windows checkouts.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files must never be line-ending normalised.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gz binary
*.zip binary
*.whl binary
